                <pb facs="0675" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg595"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Powell.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May 19,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hill replies in the negative to Mr. Powell’s request to be permitted to take
                    the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Topeka</hi> to St. Marc to consult with the
                    commander of the army of the north and advises him not to go to Port au Prince,
                    stating that there appears to be no occasion for Mr. Powell’s intervention.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
